<p data-start=3D"3431" data-end=3D"3607">All terms are <em data-start=3D"34=
45" data-end=3D"3473">penalties relative to SOTA</em> (best circuit so far)=
. If you beat or match SOTA in a metric, that term is zero or negative =E2=
=86=92 <code data-start=3D"3568" data-end=3D"3579">max(0, =E2=80=A6)</code>=
 clamps to 0, so no penalty.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3609" data-end=3D"3628">They also describe:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3630" data-end=3D"3990">
<li data-start=3D"3630" data-end=3D"3754">
<p data-start=3D"3632" data-end=3D"3754">Storage: circuit files live in R2/=
S3, and miners provide URLs; validators use <strong data-start=3D"3710" dat=
a-end=3D"3725">signed URLs</strong> / HTTP download to get them.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3755" data-end=3D"3912">
<p data-start=3D"3757" data-end=3D"3912"><strong data-start=3D"3757" data-e=
nd=3D"3771">Commitment</strong>: they anchor the <code data-start=3D"3789" =
data-end=3D"3797">SHA256</code> of <code data-start=3D"3801" data-end=3D"38=
17">model.compiled</code> on-chain and ensure that what they download match=
es the on-chain commitment before evaluating.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3913" data-end=3D"3990">
<p data-start=3D"3915" data-end=3D"3990">Platform: again, arm64 macOS is th=
e =E2=80=9Ccanonical=E2=80=9D environment for evaluation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3992" data-end=3D"4094">So: docs and code are consistent =
=E2=80=94 this is <em data-start=3D"4035" data-end=3D"4041">very</em> SOTA-=
relative, incentivizing continuous improvement.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4096" data-end=3D"4099">
<h2 data-start=3D"4101" data-end=3D"4137">3. Validator competition pipeline=
</h2>
