<h3 data-start=3D"12699" data-end=3D"12732">5.3. New circuit/proof system</=
h3>
<ul data-start=3D"12734" data-end=3D"13031">
<li data-start=3D"12734" data-end=3D"12891">
<p data-start=3D"12736" data-end=3D"12784">Under <code data-start=3D"12742"=
 data-end=3D"12783">neurons/execution_layer/proof_handlers/</code>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"12788" data-end=3D"12891">
<li data-start=3D"12788" data-end=3D"12891">
<p data-start=3D"12790" data-end=3D"12800">There are:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"12805" data-end=3D"12891">
<li data-start=3D"12805" data-end=3D"12824">
<p data-start=3D"12807" data-end=3D"12824"><code data-start=3D"12807" data-=
end=3D"12824">base_handler.py</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"12829" data-end=3D"12848">
<p data-start=3D"12831" data-end=3D"12848"><code data-start=3D"12831" data-=
end=3D"12848">ezkl_handler.py</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"12853" data-end=3D"12872">
<p data-start=3D"12855" data-end=3D"12872"><code data-start=3D"12855" data-=
end=3D"12872">jolt_handler.py</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"12877" data-end=3D"12891">
<p data-start=3D"12879" data-end=3D"12891"><code data-start=3D"12879" data-=
end=3D"12891">factory.py</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"12893" data-end=3D"13031">
<p data-start=3D"12895" data-end=3D"13031">You could add <code data-start=
=3D"12909" data-end=3D"12924">my_handler.py</code>, register it in <code da=
ta-start=3D"12941" data-end=3D"12953">factory.py</code>, and extend <code d=
ata-start=3D"12966" data-end=3D"12979">ProofSystem</code> enum in <code dat=
a-start=3D"12988" data-end=3D"13016">execution_layer/circuit.py</code> to s=
upport it.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"13033" data-end=3D"13154">Then the miner=E2=80=99s <code d=
ata-start=3D"13050" data-end=3D"13072">VerifiedModelSession</code> can pick=
 your proof system, and competition evaluator can call the right handler.</=
p>
<hr data-start=3D"13156" data-end=3D"13159">
<h2 data-start=3D"13161" data-end=3D"13197">6. Things I=E2=80=99d watch / s=
uggestions</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"13199" data-end=3D"13227">6.1. Timeouts &amp; blocking</h=
3>
<ul data-start=3D"13229" data-end=3D"13523">
<li data-start=3D"13229" data-end=3D"13523">
<p data-start=3D"13231" data-end=3D"13265">Validator competition thread use=
s:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"13269" data-end=3D"13523">
<li data-start=3D"13269" data-end=3D"13449">
<p data-start=3D"13271" data-end=3D"13449"><code data-start=3D"13271" data-=
end=3D"13301">loop.run_until_complete(...)</code> inside a thread =E2=86=92=
 if the async part stalls (network issues), you can block that thread for u=
p to <code data-start=3D"13399" data-end=3D"13409">ONE_HOUR</code> (downloa=
d) or <code data-start=3D"13424" data-end=3D"13438">FIVE_MINUTES</code> (pr=
oving).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"13452" data-end=3D"13523">
<p data-start=3D"13454" data-end=3D"13523">If you=E2=80=99re running many m=
iners/circuits, this might choke concurrency.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"13525" data-end=3D"13568"><strong data-start=3D"13525" dat=
a-end=3D"13539">Suggestion</strong>: if you fork this, consider:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"13570" data-end=3D"13704">
<li data-start=3D"13570" data-end=3D"13622">
<p data-start=3D"13572" data-end=3D"13622">Offloading evaluations to a sepa=
rate process pool.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"13623" data-end=3D"13704">
<p data-start=3D"13625" data-end=3D"13704">Using <code data-start=3D"13631"=
 data-end=3D"13649">asyncio.wait_for</code> around downloads + subprocesses=
 with tighter timeouts.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"13706" data-end=3D"13736">6.2. Storage &amp; credentials<=
/h3>
<ul data-start=3D"13738" data-end=3D"13976">
<li data-start=3D"13738" data-end=3D"13804">
<p data-start=3D"13740" data-end=3D"13804">Miner uses <code data-start=3D"1=
3751" data-end=3D"13758">boto3</code> directly with whatever env creds you =
give it.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"13805" data-end=3D"13976">
<p data-start=3D"13807" data-end=3D"13824">If misconfigured:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"13827" data-end=3D"13976">
<li data-start=3D"13827" data-end=3D"13895">
<p data-start=3D"13829" data-end=3D"13895">Competitions just silently fail =
to upload or provide invalid URLs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"13898" data-end=3D"13976">
<p data-start=3D"13900" data-end=3D"13976">Validator logs =E2=80=9Cfailed t=
o download=E2=80=9D but miners might not get clear feedback.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"13978" data-end=3D"13993"><strong data-start=3D"13978" dat=
a-end=3D"13992">Suggestion</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"13995" data-end=3D"14129">
<li data-start=3D"13995" data-end=3D"14129">
<p data-start=3D"13997" data-end=3D"14054">Add explicit health-check / self=
-test command for miners:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"14057" data-end=3D"14129">
<li data-start=3D"14057" data-end=3D"14129">
<p data-start=3D"14059" data-end=3D"14129">Upload a dummy circuit, ensure v=
alidator can fetch it and log success.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"14131" data-end=3D"14160">6.3. Platform assumptions</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"14162" data-end=3D"14382">
<li data-start=3D"14162" data-end=3D"14227">
<p data-start=3D"14164" data-end=3D"14227">Docs and notebooks assume macOS =
arm64, Metal acceleration, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"14228" data-end=3D"14382">
<p data-start=3D"14230" data-end=3D"14292">If you run validators elsewhere,=
 you might see differences in:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"14295" data-end=3D"14382">
<li data-start=3D"14295" data-end=3D"14333">
<p data-start=3D"14297" data-end=3D"14333">Performance metrics (response_ti=
me).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"14336" data-end=3D"14382">
<p data-start=3D"14338" data-end=3D"14382">Potential numeric quirks (but li=
kely small).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"14384" data-end=3D"14445"><strong data-start=3D"14384" dat=
a-end=3D"14405">If you adapt this</strong> to Linux validators, you might w=
ant to:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"14447" data-end=3D"14556">
<li data-start=3D"14447" data-end=3D"14477">
<p data-start=3D"14449" data-end=3D"14477">Recalibrate SOTA thresholds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"14478" data-end=3D"14556">
<p data-start=3D"14480" data-end=3D"14556">Ensure ONNX / ezkl versions are =
locked (via <code data-start=3D"14524" data-end=3D"14533">uv.lock</code> / =
<code data-start=3D"14536" data-end=3D"14554">requirements.txt</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"14558" data-end=3D"14592">6.4. Global competition config<=
/h3>
<ul data-start=3D"14594" data-end=3D"14732">
<li data-start=3D"14594" data-end=3D"14663">
<p data-start=3D"14596" data-end=3D"14663"><code data-start=3D"14596" data-=
end=3D"14616">ACTIVE_COMPETITION</code> is a single global constant in <cod=
e data-start=3D"14648" data-end=3D"14662">constants.py</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"14664" data-end=3D"14732">
<p data-start=3D"14666" data-end=3D"14732"><code data-start=3D"14666" data-=
end=3D"14693">COMPETITION_SYNC_INTERVAL</code> hard-coded at 24h =E2=86=92 =
slow SOTA updates.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"14734" data-end=3D"14772">If you want more dynamic competi=
tions:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"14774" data-end=3D"14882">
<li data-start=3D"14774" data-end=3D"14840">
<p data-start=3D"14776" data-end=3D"14840">Make <code data-start=3D"14781" =
data-end=3D"14801">ACTIVE_COMPETITION</code> read from chain or from a conf=
ig file.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"14841" data-end=3D"14882">
<p data-start=3D"14843" data-end=3D"14882">Allow interval override via env/=
config.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"14884" data-end=3D"14920">6.5. Error handling / resilienc=
e</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"14922" data-end=3D"15068">
<li data-start=3D"14922" data-end=3D"15005">
<p data-start=3D"14924" data-end=3D"15005"><code data-start=3D"14924" data-=
end=3D"14940">CircuitManager</code> logs stacktraces on download failure bu=
t mostly returns <code data-start=3D"14997" data-end=3D"15004">False</code>=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15006" data-end=3D"15068">
<p data-start=3D"15008" data-end=3D"15068"><code data-start=3D"15008" data-=
end=3D"15026">CircuitEvaluator</code> raises runtime errors for setup failu=
res.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"15070" data-end=3D"15110">This is fine for a research subn=
et, but:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"15112" data-end=3D"15199">
<li data-start=3D"15112" data-end=3D"15199">
<p data-start=3D"15114" data-end=3D"15199">For production, you might want m=
ore per-miner backoff / penalties vs hard exceptions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"15201" data-end=3D"15204">
<h2 data-start=3D"15206" data-end=3D"15230">7. Quick mental model</h2>
<p data-start=3D"15232" data-end=3D"15252">Putting it together:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"15254" data-end=3D"15790">
<li data-start=3D"15254" data-end=3D"15398">
<p data-start=3D"15256" data-end=3D"15266"><strong data-start=3D"15256" dat=
a-end=3D"15265">Miner</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"15269" data-end=3D"15398">
<li data-start=3D"15269" data-end=3D"15293">
<p data-start=3D"15271" data-end=3D"15293">Hosts model + circuit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15296" data-end=3D"15325">
<p data-start=3D"15298" data-end=3D"15325">Uploads artifacts to S3/R2.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15328" data-end=3D"15398">
<p data-start=3D"15330" data-end=3D"15398">Advertises circuit hashes and si=
gned URLs via <code data-start=3D"15376" data-end=3D"15389">Competition</co=
de> synapse.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15400" data-end=3D"15790">
<p data-start=3D"15402" data-end=3D"15416"><strong data-start=3D"15402" dat=
a-end=3D"15415">Validator</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"15419" data-end=3D"15790">
<li data-start=3D"15419" data-end=3D"15459">
<p data-start=3D"15421" data-end=3D"15459">Periodically syncs active compet=
ition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15462" data-end=3D"15725">
<p data-start=3D"15464" data-end=3D"15493">For each participating miner:</p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"15498" data-end=3D"15725">
<li data-start=3D"15498" data-end=3D"15547">
<p data-start=3D"15500" data-end=3D"15547">Downloads circuit files (via <co=
de data-start=3D"15529" data-end=3D"15545">CircuitManager</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15552" data-end=3D"15607">
<p data-start=3D"15554" data-end=3D"15607">Fetches benchmark data (via <cod=
e data-start=3D"15582" data-end=3D"15605">CompetitionDataSource</code>).</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15612" data-end=3D"15667">
<p data-start=3D"15614" data-end=3D"15667">Runs evaluation (via <code data-=
start=3D"15635" data-end=3D"15653">CircuitEvaluator</code> + ezkl/onnx).</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15672" data-end=3D"15725">
<p data-start=3D"15674" data-end=3D"15725">Updates SOTA and <code data-star=
t=3D"15691" data-end=3D"15704">NeuronState</code> (via <code data-start=3D"=
15710" data-end=3D"15723">SotaManager</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15728" data-end=3D"15790">
<p data-start=3D"15730" data-end=3D"15790">Feeds resulting scores into over=
all reward/scoring pipeline.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"15792" data-end=3D"15795">
<p data-start=3D"15797" data-end=3D"15877">If you want, next step we can zo=
om <strong data-start=3D"15832" data-end=3D"15845">very deep</strong> into =
any particular area, e.g.:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"15879" data-end=3D"16136" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-=
only-node=3D"">
<li data-start=3D"15879" data-end=3D"15963">
<p data-start=3D"15881" data-end=3D"15963">The exact evaluation logic insid=
e <code data-start=3D"15915" data-end=3D"15933">CircuitEvaluator</code> (in=
nards of ONNX/ezkl calls).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"15964" data-end=3D"16052">
<p data-start=3D"15966" data-end=3D"16052">How the SOTA score feeds into th=
e global <code data-start=3D"16007" data-end=3D"16022">score_manager</code>=
 and eventually TAO emissions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"16053" data-end=3D"16136" data-is-last-node=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"16055" data-end=3D"16136" data-is-last-node=3D"">Or how yo=
u would wire <em data-start=3D"16077" data-end=3D"16087">your own</em> cust=
