<p data-start=3D"2280" data-end=3D"2327">It is a <strong data-start=3D"2288=
" data-end=3D"2306">packaging tool</strong>, not a proving tool.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2329" data-end=3D"2332">
<h1 data-start=3D"2334" data-end=3D"2366">=F0=9F=A7=A9 <strong data-start=
=3D"2339" data-end=3D"2366">Why do YOU not need it?</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"2368" data-end=3D"2418">Because your miner uses <strong da=
ta-start=3D"2392" data-end=3D"2410">CircuitManager</strong>, which:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2420" data-end=3D"2545">
<li data-start=3D"2420" data-end=3D"2443">
<p data-start=3D"2422" data-end=3D"2443">Hashes your circuit</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2444" data-end=3D"2467">
<p data-start=3D"2446" data-end=3D"2467">Uploads it to S3/R2</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2468" data-end=3D"2499">
<p data-start=3D"2470" data-end=3D"2499">Advertises it to validators</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2500" data-end=3D"2545">
<p data-start=3D"2502" data-end=3D"2545">Manages all circuit syncing automa=
tically</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2547" data-end=3D"2626">And validators will compile nothin=
g =E2=80=94 they just verify + evaluate your circuit.</p>
